### Summary of changes

**`project.js` — `searchMentions`:**
- Added an early return `if (!query || query.trim().length < 3) return []` at the top of `searchMentions`
- Added `minMatchCharLength: 3` to the Fuse.js options so even if the guard is bypassed, Fuse itself won't count token matches shorter than 3 chars

**`Chat.vue` — `runIntelliSense`:**
- Extracts `rawQuery` (stripping leading `@`) before the length check, so `@ab` correctly counts as 2 chars and is rejected

**`Chat.vue` — `loadMentionSuggestions`:**
- Added `if (query.length < 3) return` after slicing off the `@`, so the `@mention` dropdown also respects the 3-char minimum

